{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas","id":15190,"title":"Weird Exigent Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-21T00:11:26-08:00","id":15190,"title":"Weird Exigent Ideas","content":"So last night Hucksters came up in conversation on IRC (credit to Flare for getting the ball rolling with this).<br /> For those who've aren't familiar with the RPG Deadlands they're an interesting flavour of spellcasters who draw their power from playing games of Poker with evil spirits. If they win a hand then they get to use the spirit's essence to power a spell and the rules use a deck of playing cards. It's certainly stylistic enough to warrant it's own rules and charmset. However, having to crack out some playing cards when everyone else is just spending essence and rolling dice might be a little too convoluted while simply using poker hands as an aesthetic doesn't seem to be making the most of the idea.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Anyone else have weird ideas they want to share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T01:52:38-08:00","id":15246,"title":"","content":"Well... first of all, I would not make them Exigents I think.Not if you want to stay true to the complete concept that is. Hucksters could fit the Exalted setting very well as mortals who make deals with malevolent spirits, literally the way they do in Deadlands. You have these spirits granting them the use of powers through blessings etc.but it comes at a price. The characters make deals with these spirits through gambles, and every time they lose the gamble the spirit takes a bit of their life or sanity. Hucksters are an archetype that doesn't really befit the Exalted, it is power at a great personal risk/cost for the user, where Exaltation is power at a great cost for the benefactor.<br /> <br /> Since you're in houserule land with this one, I would simply go with putting the deck of cards on the table and convert the Deal with the Devil table for appropriate use in Exalted. The card mechanic is cool enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/628-lord-stone","name":"Lord Stone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T02:31:59-08:00","id":15269,"title":"","content":"I have had similar ideas for involving different kinds of resolution mechanics, of which cards was one idea. It can be beneficially explored.<br /> <br /> I've also had an idea about an Exigent who merges with Elementals to gain elemental powers, inspired much by the first Avatar in Legend of Korra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T03:42:21-08:00","id":15281,"title":"","content":"Exigent of Chairs.<br /> <br /> Chair dancing, hitting wrestlers with chairs, sitting on one hell of a chair...the possibilities are...okay they are somewhat limited. But I'm willing to milk it for all it's worth. I have two cows, and they are both excellent chairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly KingCrazyGenius. Still a <b><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">Malfean Bovine.</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/15221-the-new-adventures-of-spearpsycho-soulshitterson\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">The New Adventures of Spearpsycho Soulshitterson</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1253-anthonox","name":"Anthonox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1253_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:51:17-08:00","id":15310,"title":"","content":"Had a similar idea about Exalts who don't respire essence but gain it by making deals with Gods, Demons and other Exalt types. They're a lost exaltation and their Patron is only known to them, because any attempt to speak their name to anyone but another Vanij'a it will just be filtered out, like even the memory of how to say said god's name was devoured.<br /> <br /> This and the fact to most methods of tracking Exalted, they appear to be mortals, means there's a fair bit of distrust between them and Yu Shan, though there presence there is allowed and at least somewhat tolerated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T11:34:31-08:00","id":15501,"title":"","content":"Weird sorta Exigent idea:<br /> <br /> First...<br /> The inclusion of Exigents is a great idea. It fills the void that Devil Tigers will leave and it seems they'll make custom charm crafting even more interesting and fun. So as a game addition they are surely a great concept for the edition. <br /> <br /> And!<br /> We also know that Autochthonia and the Alchemicals will once again be considered as an isolated setting apart from Creation ( of course without negating the possibility of opening the bridge between both realms of existence in game).<br /> <br /> Something to keep in mind...<br /> I remember John talking about new Magical Materials in Ex3. Maybe the definition of Magical Material is different now and it is not a set of six materials but a category in which numerous other materials can be made to fit if conditions are met. <br /> <br /> So...<br /> Do you think the good Exigents idea will be &quot;excluded&quot; from the very good setting of Autochthonia? Or maybe, just maybe will the &quot;Exigent customization fun&quot; could be integrated into the Alchemicals setting, by adding NEW ALCHEMICAL CASTES based on the hypothetical new Magical Materials...<br /> <br /> But of course I, like Jon Snow, know nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:22:52-08:00","id":15573,"title":"","content":"Barring significant changes to Autochthonia, I don't think it really can include exigents. Autochthonia lacks true gods; instead it has Otto's devas and the ex machina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly KingCrazyGenius. Still a <b><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">Malfean Bovine.</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/15221-the-new-adventures-of-spearpsycho-soulshitterson\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">The New Adventures of Spearpsycho Soulshitterson</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1253-anthonox","name":"Anthonox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1253_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:48:54-08:00","id":15601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anthonox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=15573#post15573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring significant changes to Autochthonia, I don't think it really can include exigents. Autochthonia lacks true gods; instead it has Otto's devas and the ex machina.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's exactly my point. Given that they can't &quot;appropiately&quot; be there. I was imagining a way to include &quot;what makes them good&quot; by other means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:59:58-08:00","id":15609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anthonox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=15573#post15573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring significant changes to Autochthonia, I don't think it really can include exigents. Autochthonia lacks true gods; instead it has Otto's devas and the ex machina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because Sol came up with Exigence on the Creation-side of the Seal of Eight Divinities doesn't mean no one can find a similar way to create Exalts on the other side of the Seal. Third Edition will probably see my Domini moved to a type of proto-Exigent for better integration with the rule set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:03:41-08:00","id":15649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=15601#post15601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's exactly my point. Given that they can't &quot;appropiately&quot; be there. I was imagining a way to include &quot;what makes them good&quot; by other means.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's likely an attempt to stick firmly to the definition of &quot;Exigent.&quot; I've seen the misconception flying around that &quot;Exigent&quot; is a synonym for &quot;Custom Exalt,&quot; when the former is a subset of the latter created through a particular method. Both should be seen as just as legitimate and valid. I don't even personally have a problem if people want to use &quot;Exigent&quot; as an informal term for custom Exalts, as long as they know the distinction. It's just that, particularly at present with the only clarifications existing in EX3 Team comments scattered hither and yon (or compiled in the What We Know Wiki and Nishkriya, neither of which is as known as it is valuable), I think it's a worthwhile clarification to make, just in case.<br /> <br /> As for your idea, it could be cool! I'm not sure it would necessarily appear in a book,* but it could be fertile ground for homebrew. If there's a good idea for a niche that the other 6 castes don't presently fill, could be very neat indeed.<br /> <br /> * Mainly from the impression I got that Alchemicals and Autochthonia would not be changing drastically. I might have read something incorrectly, though, and there's still some years before EX3 visits them again for minds to change, but hey!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:18:08-08:00","id":15665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=15649#post15649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Mainly from the impression I got that Alchemicals and Autochthonia would not be changing drastically. I might have read something incorrectly, though, and there's still some years before EX3 visits them again for minds to change, but hey!</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion is that it would be disapointing to not see anything new on Ex3's Autochthonia. We'll see of course.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:25:13-08:00","id":15672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anthonox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=15573#post15573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring significant changes to Autochthonia, I don't think it really can include exigents. Autochthonia lacks true gods; instead it has Otto's devas and the ex machina.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Autochthon pioneered the creation of Exaltations and taught the secret to the Celestial Incarnae, it ought to be plausible that Autochthon's own Third Circle Souls are capable of figuring out how to make their own Exaltations, if they don't already know how.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T16:34:33-08:00","id":15702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=15665#post15665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion is that it would be disapointing to not see anything new on Ex3's Autochthonia. We'll see of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, the impression I get is more that the EX3 Team is now getting to re-imagine all the Exalted splats and the setting as a whole around them from 2e's, so drastic changes are to be expected. Said Team has already done that sort of re-imagining for Alchemicals and Autochthonia -- which has (in theory) &quot;a closed circle cut off from Creation&quot; as part of its premise -- so it may not see the same sort of drastic changes. I still fully expect to see new Autochthonia/Alchemical stuff.<br /> <br /> Not least because the Team's stated aim in location-based books in EX3 is not to simply retread previous editions' material as 2e did a lot. They would certainly include a ton of new stuff were they to do a new Autochthonia book. There was also the floating of a possible Alchemical presence in Creation sometime in the distant past; that could point to all sorts of new things and possibilities. I just don't presently expect the core ideas to change much at all because they already work great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T22:32:44-08:00","id":15898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Stone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=15246#post15246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hucksters could fit the Exalted setting very well as mortals who make deals with malevolent spirits, literally the way they do in Deadlands. You have these spirits granting them the use of powers through blessings etc.but it comes at a price.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hexes aren't blessings from the Manitou, they're the result of the Huckster learning to shape its power into a desirable form (hence why they learn new ones like spells).<br /> By 3e standards that's basically a form of sorcery with the spirit supplying the essence to the spell if it loses the wager. That has the potential to be extremely powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Stone</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hucksters are an archetype that doesn't really befit the Exalted, it is power at a great personal risk/cost for the user, where Exaltation is power at a great cost for the benefactor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking gambling with high stakes would be something inherent to the hypothetical benefactor's nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 11-22-2013, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T12:07:42-08:00","id":16219,"title":"","content":"I will probably port over the Khaucon as some sort of Exigents of the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> But I do have an idea for a custom exalt whose Exaltation is <i>outside</i> their body; instead of improving themselves, they improve the stuff they make.<br /> <br /> Kinda like clockworkers in Unknown Armies.<br /> <br /> Actually, doing up Adepts as a form of Exalted would be neat; you could use Motes in place of Minor Charges and Willpower in place of Significant Charges... Dunno what Major Charges would be, though.<br /> <br /> Because, come on, who wouldn't want to play an Irascimancer in Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:44:02-08:00","id":16359,"title":"","content":"I think that if you wanted to make this an actual exigent it'd need a fair bit of reworking, but the basic idea is badass. You could also make it some kind of sub-Exaltation powerset (given via Endowment, maybe?) or maybe do it via one of those black market exigents that's passed through many hands. Poker's kinda off-theme for Exalted, though -- cards in general feel a bit too &quot;eurofantasy&quot;. The oldest games of chance we know about seemed to involve dice and other &quot;casting&quot; games of that sort, though it could just be that those are the most likely to leave an archaeological record. It kind of blows the aesthetic to be using dice that way in a dice-based RPG, though. I think for a Huckster expy I'd probably use some kind of tile game, like dominoes or mahjongg.<br /> <br /> My most out-there Exigent idea is one where multiple people (implicitly, all the PCs) share a single Exaltation behind them, and their powers facilitate teamwork but require sharing and coordination. Not sure what god I'd want that to key off of, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:30:47-08:00","id":16391,"title":"","content":"I've got an idea for a highlander-esqe Exigent of Consumption that kills other Exigents and takes their powers. Would probably acquire the downsides of the &quot;black market&quot; exigencies as it killed more Exigents, just like one made via passing through multiple gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:46:49-08:00","id":16402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=16391#post16391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got an idea for a highlander-esqe Exigent of Consumption that kills other Exigents and takes their powers. Would probably acquire the downsides of the &quot;black market&quot; exigencies as it killed more Exigents, just like one made via passing through multiple gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Highlander, or <i>Heroes</i> Sylar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:52:33-08:00","id":16405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=16402#post16402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Highlander, or <i>Heroes</i> Sylar?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't watch Heroes. Does Sylar pull the Rogue/Ms. Marvel thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:55:23-08:00","id":16406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=16405#post16405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't watch Heroes. Does Sylar pull the Rogue/Ms. Marvel thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't watch it either, but I believe he does it in a more permanent manner. Brain eating or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly KingCrazyGenius. Still a <b><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">Malfean Bovine.</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/15221-the-new-adventures-of-spearpsycho-soulshitterson\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">The New Adventures of Spearpsycho Soulshitterson</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1253-anthonox","name":"Anthonox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1253_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:57:00-08:00","id":16407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anthonox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=16406#post16406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't watch it either, but I believe he does it in a more permanent manner. Brain eating or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Rogue has stolen powers permanently, in particular with Ms. Marvel. That said, yes, that's the idea although it wouldn't be through brain eating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T19:02:09-08:00","id":16413,"title":"","content":"It was only ever implied that Sylar ate the brains. When actually called on that, Sylar said the idea was disgusting.<br /> <br /> Since his original power was to understand how something worked by looking at its innards (like a broken clock), it's been speculated that he was poking directly at people's brains to reverse-engineer their powers.<br /> <br /> But that's as much as I want to talk about a disgusting character from a boring TV show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T19:27:43-08:00","id":16423,"title":"","content":"I actually kinda have a soft spot for the first season. Not so much the second. I'm particularly glad I stopped since I heard it got stupider and stupider from there. But yeah, studying them was the impression I got. In a way, it would have made for a cool contrast, given how they had seemed to imply Peter Patrelli's power worked:* Sylar would have needed to physically open people up to understand and duplicate how they worked, Peter would have needed to understand someone emotionally and personally for such duplication.<br /> <br /> * I remember a lot of talk about how it was rooted in love, before they apparently decided &quot;Nope! He just gets everything he's near.&quot; Unless I'm wrong on any point; my memory's imperfect here and I don't care enough to look it up.<br /> <br /> But yes! Onto better topics.<br /> <br /> I'll be interested to see how an idea like Lafing Cat's would work out. Particularly with regard to non-Charm stuff; juggling anima banners/powers, non-Charm powers (a la Lunar shapeshifting, Sidereal Astrology, or Getimian Alchemy), Limit or analogue thereof, other foundational changes/capacities an Exigency works in its Chosen... Interesting possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T19:53:03-08:00","id":16436,"title":"","content":"The Ar Tonelico games are apparently a mixed bag of good ideas and poor implementation (though I hear the second is better), but I'd like to find various ways to represent the Reyvateils.<br /> <br /> Solars and Terrestrials with Performance Charms, possibly Sidereals with Silver-Voiced Nightengale Style and an appropriate Sidereal Martial Art, Alchemicals with musical and sorcerous Charms equipped, and Chosen of Songs Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T05:50:13-08:00","id":17092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=15609#post15609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because Sol came up with Exigence on the Creation-side of the Seal of Eight Divinities doesn't mean no one can find a similar way to create Exalts on the other side of the Seal. Third Edition will probably see my Domini moved to a type of proto-Exigent for better integration with the rule set.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be interesting to explore the impact of new Exalts upon Autochthonian culture without simultaneously piling on the massive culture shock of re-establishing contact with Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T06:22:26-08:00","id":17100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anthonox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/15190-weird-exigent-ideas?p=15281#post15281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigent of Chairs.<br /> <br /> Chair dancing, hitting wrestlers with chairs, sitting on one hell of a chair...the possibilities are...okay they are somewhat limited. But I'm willing to milk it for all it's worth. I have two cows, and they are both excellent chairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... <br /> <br /> &quot;I am the perfect rider who can never be dismounted, because I imbue my mount with the Essence of Chairness, and the bond between chair and chair-sitter can nevah be broke!&quot;? <br /> <br /> &quot;I can claim the powers of the throne, because what is it but a chair?&quot;?<br /> <br /> &quot;Making people want to sit the hell down&quot;?<br /> <br /> &quot;Reading people's personalities and motivations through their armchair bumprint&quot;?<br /> <br /> &quot;Sanitation magic (because Elvis is the King and his throne has its own power)&quot;?<br /> <br /> Long live the Chairklaive!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}